### 10. `compliance_guidelines.docx` (as TXT)

TRANSACTION MANAGEMENT COMPLIANCE GUIDELINES
=============================================

EFFECTIVE DATE: January 2024
DOCUMENT CLASS: INTERNAL USE ONLY

1. ANTI-MONEY LAUNDERING (AML) REQUIREMENTS
--------------------------------------------
- All transactions above PKR 5,000,000 require manual review
- Customer identification mandatory before transaction processing
- Quarterly risk assessment for all customer accounts
- Reporting of suspicious transactions to FIU (Financial Intelligence Unit)
- Sanctions list screening for all international transactions

2. KNOW YOUR CUSTOMER (KYC) POLICY
----------------------------------
- KYC verification mandatory for all transactions above PKR 1,000,000
- Enhanced KYC for PEPs (Politically Exposed Persons)
- Annual KYC refresh required
- Source of funds verification for large deposits

3. TRANSACTION LIMITS & CONTROLS
---------------------------------
Daily Transaction Limit: PKR 50,000,000
Monthly Transaction Limit: PKR 500,000,000
Single Transaction Limit: PKR 25,000,000
Unusual Activity Threshold: 150% of customer's 90-day average

4. FRAUD PREVENTION MEASURES
-----------------------------
- Real-time transaction monitoring
- Machine learning-based anomaly detection
- Customer verification for transactions above threshold
- SMS confirmation for high-value transactions
- Auto-block on suspicious patterns (3 declined attempts = 24hr block)

5. REPORTING REQUIREMENTS
-------------------------
- Daily transaction reports to Compliance Department
- Weekly fraud analysis reports
- Monthly KYC compliance reports
- Quarterly regulatory reporting to SBP
- Annual audit by external auditors

6. DISPUTE RESOLUTION
---------------------
- Customer disputes must be filed within 90 days
- Investigation period: 30 days
- Reversal processing: 3-5 business days
- Customer notification mandatory

7. DATA SECURITY & PRIVACY
--------------------------
- All transaction data encrypted (AES-256)
- Access logs maintained for all transactions
- Customer data retention: 7 years post-account closure
- PII masking in all reports and communications

8. SANCTIONS & EMBARGO COMPLIANCE
----------------------------------
- OFAC (Office of Foreign Assets Control) screening mandatory
- UN Sanctions list verification
- Pakistan's FIA sanctions list screening
- Real-time screening for international transactions